    "title": "At risk man is missing in Fresno and police need your help to find him - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christian Valdez ,\n2 hours ago FRESNO, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) - The Fresno Police Department has asked the community to help find a missing 39-year-old at-risk man on Thursday.\nIsrael Garcia is the 39-year-old who went missing on Wednesday morning, according to officials.\nPolice say he was last seen on Wednesday at 8 a.m. near the 4900 block of Holt Avenue, which is not too far from Shaw and Marks avenues.\nOfficers say Garcia was wearing a black sweater, gray sweatpants, and gray Nike shoes. Garcia is 5 feet 3 inches tall and weighs 210 pounds. He has short black hair and black eyes.\nIf you have any information that can help police find him, please call the Fresno Police Department at 559-621-7000.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to YourCentralValley.com | CBS47 and KSEE24.",
